# No `gspp_impl_*` in `### Rules:`

Narrative seeds (`gspp_impl_*`) exist only so CSV → OSCAL keeps an
implemented-requirement when no ComplianceAsCode rule binds. They are **helpers**,
not real rules.

## Required

- **Never** put `gspp_impl_*` under markdown `### Rules:`.
- Seed-only controls: omit the `### Rules:` heading (or leave it empty of
  bullets). Frontmatter may still list the seed for trestle — that is OK.
- `### Rules:` lists **CaC rule ids only**.
- Never cite `gspp_impl_*` in German implementation prose.

## After regenerate

If `regenerate_components.sh` / trestle writes `gspp_impl_*` into `### Rules:`,
**remove those bullets** (and the heading if nothing CaC remains) before commit.

## Consistency check

Listing `gspp_impl_*` under `### Rules:` is a **CRITICAL** display defect.
Missing `### Rules:` on a seed-only control (CSV/JSON seed present) is **not**
a defect.
